\pard\fi0\li0\qj\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 1r-64v 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\qj\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\qj\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 content:
\par \pard\li720\fi-360\jclisttab\tx0\qj\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 {\listtext\pard\plain\f4\fs24\lang1024 \u-4051 ?\tab}\ls8\ilvl0 Alfasi\lquote s work is a compendium/abridgement of the Babylonian and Palestinian Talmud; the present codex contains the following parts [orthography adapted (as far as possible) to modern usage and GND respectively]:
\plain\par \pard\li1080\fi-360\jclisttab\tx0\qj\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 {\listtext\pard\plain\f4\fs24\lang1024 \u-4051 ?\tab}\ls8\ilvl1 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 end of the Cod. \u701 ?Eruvin DelitzschD: \u8222 \'84Erubin\ldblquote ) [{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 GND: \u701 ?Eruvin, 4408687-8}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ]
\plain\par {\listtext\pard\plain\f4\fs24\lang1024 \u-4051 ?\tab}\ls8\ilvl1 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 Masekhet Pesa\u7717 ?im DelitzschD: \u8222 \'84Masikta Pesahim\ldblquote ) - Talmud tractate on Pessach; [GND: {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[1].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Talmud, 16. Pesa\u7717 ?im; 1089087683}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ]
\plain\par {\listtext\pard\plain\f4\fs24\lang1024 \u-4051 ?\tab}\ls8\ilvl1 {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[8].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Hilkhot Yom ha-Kippurim}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (Delitzsch: \u8222 \'84Hilkot Joma (Jom ha-Kippurim)\rdblquote )
\plain\par {\listtext\pard\plain\f4\fs24\lang1024 \u-4051 ?\tab}\ls8\ilvl1 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 (probably)\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  GND: {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[2].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Talmud Yeru\u353 \'9aalmi, 19. Sukka, 1089092490}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   (Delitzsch: \u8222 \'84Suka\ldblquote )
\plain\par {\listtext\pard\plain\f4\fs24\lang1024 \u-4051 ?\tab}\ls8\ilvl1 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 GND: {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[3].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Talmud, 20. Beitsah, 1089088795}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   (Delitzsch: \u8222 \'84Be\u231 \'e7a (Jom Thob)\ldblquote )
\plain\par {\listtext\pard\plain\f4\fs24\lang1024 \u-4051 ?\tab}\ls8\ilvl1 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 GND: {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[4].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Talmud Yeru\u353 \'9aalmi, 22. Ta\u703 ?anit, 1089092636}}\plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24   \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (Delitzsch: \u8222 \'84Ta\u700 'anit\ldblquote )
\plain\par {\listtext\pard\plain\f4\fs24\lang1024 \u-4051 ?\tab}\ls8\ilvl1 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 GND: {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[5].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Talmud Yeru\u353 \'9aalmi, 21. R\u244 \'f4s ha\u353 \'9a-\u353 \'9aana, 1089092431}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (Delitzsch: \u8222 \'84Rosh ha-Shana\ldblquote )
\plain\par {\listtext\pard\plain\f4\fs24\lang1024 \u-4051 ?\tab}\ls8\ilvl1 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 GND: {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[6].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Talmud, 23. Megilla, 1089092741}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (Delitzsch: \u8222 \'84Megila\ldblquote )
\plain\par {\listtext\pard\plain\f4\fs24\lang1024 \u-4051 ?\tab}\ls8\ilvl1 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 GND: {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[7].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Talmud. Mo\u703 ?ed \u7731 ?a\u7789 ?an, 1088071104}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (Delitzsch: \u8222 \'84Mo\u235 \'ebd Qathan\ldblquote )
\plain\par \pard\fi0\li0\qj\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 
\par \pard\li720\fi-360\jclisttab\tx0\qj\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 {\listtext\pard\plain\f4\fs24\lang1024 \u-4051 ?\tab}\ls8\ilvl0 within the commentary several people are praised
\plain\par \pard\fi0\li0\qj\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\qj\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 David, Die hebr\u228 \'e4ische Handschriftensammlung, \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 S. 309: \u8222 \'84{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[9].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Sefer ha-Halachot}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  (Buch der Pflichten) wurde von {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[0].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 R. Jitzchak ben Ja\rquote akov Alfasi}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 , bekannt als Rif, der im 11. Jahrhundert in Nordafrika und Spanien lebte, verfasst. Er stellte ein umfassendes Kompendium halachischen Materials aus dem Talmud zusammen. Die Leipziger Handschrift enth\u228 \'e4lt lediglich den Abschnitt zur Ordnung \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Moe\rquote d\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  (Festzeiten). Sie entstand im 14. Jahrhundert (B\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 .H. 5).\ldblquote }

