\par \pard\fi0\li720\qj\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 content:
\par \pard\li720\fi-360\jclisttab\tx0\qj\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 {\listtext\pard\plain\f4\fs24\lang1024 \u-4051 ?\tab}\ls1\ilvl0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 official title of the work: {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f3\lang1037\fs24\chcbpat17 \u1506 \'f2\u1502 \'ee\u1493 \'e5\u1491 \'e3\u1497 \'e9 \u1490 \'e2\u1493 \'e5\u1500 \'ec\u1492 \'e4}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (\u8222 \'84pillars of exile\ldblquote ), completed in 1277
\plain\par {\listtext\pard\plain\f4\fs24\lang1024 \u-4051 ?\tab}\ls1\ilvl0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 author of the work: Isaac ben Joseph of Corbeil (gest. 1280) (lat.: Isaak Corbelensis) (GND: {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[0].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Yits\u7717 ?a\u7731 ? Ben-Yosef, Corbeil, 138532982}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 )
\plain\par {\listtext\pard\plain\f4\fs24\lang1024 \u-4051 ?\tab}\ls1\ilvl0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 in the end there are several little poems written by Isaac himself, all assigned to the particular sections into which the book is divided
\plain\par \pard\fi0\li0\qj\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\qj\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 AD, S. 310: \u8222 \'84Die Handschrift {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[1].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Sefer Mitzvot Katan}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (Kleines Buch der Gebote), abgek\u252 \'fcrzt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Semak\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , auch unter dem Titel \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Amudei Gola\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (S\u228 \'e4ulen der Diaspora) bekannt, entstand im Jahre 1305 (B.H. 9). Ihr Autor ist R. Jitzchak ben Joseph von Corbeil, ein franz\u246 \'f6sischer Rabbiner, Gelehrter und Tossafist.\ldblquote }

