\par \pard\li720\fi-360\jclisttab\tx0\qj\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 {\listtext\pard\plain\f1\fs24\lang1033 -\tab}\ls3\ilvl0 all of the books were written by one scribe 
\plain\par \pard\fi0\li720\qj\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (\u8222 \'84uno eodemque a librario ad unum omnes exarati\ldblquote )
\par \pard\li720\fi-360\jclisttab\tx0\qj\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 {\listtext\pard\plain\f1\fs24\lang1033 -\tab}\ls3\ilvl0 bought in 1518 by {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[0].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Juda ben Sabatai}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  for 125 coins (\u8222 \'84pretio centum viginti quinque nummum\ldblquote ) 
\plain\par {\listtext\pard\plain\f1\fs24\lang1033 -\tab}\ls3\ilvl0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 the codex bears great resemblance to the one in the \u8222 \'84Bibliothecae Taurinensis\ldblquote  (library of Turin) described by Wolfius (IV. p. 751) but is \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 not\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  identical to it}

