\pard\fi0\li0\qj\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\fs24 history:
\par \pard\li1080\fi-360\jclisttab\tx0\qj\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 {\listtext\pard\plain\f7\fs24\lang1024 \u-4051 ?\tab}\ls4\ilvl1 14\plain \f4\lang1033\fs16 th\plain \f1\fs24  century (David, Die hebr\u228 \'e4ischen Handschriften, S. 308)
\plain\par {\listtext\pard\plain\f7\fs24\lang1024 \u-4051 ?\tab}\ls4\ilvl1 \plain \f1\fs24 maybe made for private and not for synagogal use (Delitzsch, Codices, S. 275)
\plain\par {\listtext\pard\plain\f7\fs24\lang1024 \u-4051 ?\tab}\ls4\ilvl1 \plain \f1\fs24 brought from Italy (s. entries by readers dating back to the first third of the 17\plain \f4\lang1033\fs16 th\plain \f1\fs24  century; fol. 204 b)
\plain\par {\listtext\pard\plain\f7\fs24\lang1024 \u-4051 ?\tab}\ls4\ilvl1 \plain \f1\fs24 Wagenseil [GND: {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[0].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f4\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17\cf1 Wagenseil,\~Johann Christoph; 119090198}}\plain \f4\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 ]\plain \f1\fs24  bought it, along with two other manuscripts (\u8222 \'84Be\u235 \'ebr Gola\ldblquote , \u8222 \'84Misle Sandabar\ldblquote ) in Moravia (\u8222 \'84Niclasburgi\ldblquote  \u8594 ? German \u8222 \'84Nikolsburg\ldblquote , today \u8222 \'84Mikulov\ldblquote ; starting in the late Middle Ages it was home to an important Jewish community; GND: Nikolsburg; 4075404-2), from a [FD] \u8222 \'84uneducated Jew\ldblquote  (\u8222 \'84de Judaeo indocto\ldblquote ) as he narrates himself in his \u8222 \'84Epistola de Hydraspide\ldblquote 
\plain\par {\listtext\pard\plain\f7\fs24\lang1024 \u-4051 ?\tab}\ls4\ilvl1 \plain \f1\fs24 as some suppose the codex had once been in the possession of an Oriental Karaite (\u8222 \'84in manibus Karaitae orientalis olim fuisse\ldblquote )}

