\plain\par \pard\li1080\fi-360\jclisttab\tx0\qj\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 {\listtext\pard\plain\f3\fs24\lang1024 \u-4051 ?\tab}\ls3\ilvl1 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 scribe: {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[0].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Adonia Klomiti ben-Aba Klomiti}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (aus Thessaloniki) (David: R. Adonja ben Abba Calomiti; Saloniki 1329)
\plain\par \pard\fi0\li0\qj\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (\plain \f2\fs24 \u1488 ?\u1491 ?\u1493 ?\u1504 ?\u1497 ?\u1492 ? \u1511 ?\u1500 ?\u1493 ?\u1502 ?\u1497 ?\u1496 ?\u1497 ? \u1489 ?\u1503 ? \u1492 ?\u1504 ?\u1490 ?\u1497 ?\u1491 ? \u1492 ?\u1512 ?\u1488 ?\u1513 ? \u1492 ?\u1504 ?\u1489 ?\u1493 ?\u1503 ? \u1493 ?\u1492 ?\u1502 ?\u1513 ?\u1499 ?\u1497 ?\u1500 ? \u1499 ?\u1489 ?\u1493 ?\u1491 ? \u1502 ?\u1512 ? \u1493 ?\u1512 ?\u1489 ?\u1497 ? \u1488 ?\u1489 ?\u1488 ? \u1511 ?\u1500 ?\u1493 ?\u1502 ?\u1497 ?\u1496 ?\u1497 ?\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 )
\par \pard\fi0\li0\qj\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 - completion of the text: \plain \f2\fs24 \u1489 ?\u1497 ?\u1493 ?\u1501 ? \u1488 ?' \u1489 ?' \u1500 ?\u1495 ?\u1491 ?\u1513 ? \u1488 ?\u1497 ?\u1497 ?\u1512 ? \u1513 ?\u1504 ?\u1514 ? \u1492 ?''\u1508 ?\u1496 ? \u1500 ?\u1497 ?\u1510 ?\u1497 ?\u1512 ?\u1492 ?
\par \pard\fi0\li0\qj\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (\plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24 1329\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 .) in \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24 Saloniki\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (\plain \f2\fs24 \u1513 ?\u1500 ?\u1493 ?\u1504 ?\u1497 ?\u1511 ?\u1497 ?\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) (fol. 18v) \u8594 ? the same information on name and date appear again on fol. 58b [\u8230 \'85] and the name itself as an acrostichon on fol. 173v
\par \pard\fi0\li0\qj\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\qj\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 [David's contradiction, David, Die hebr\u228 \'e4ischen Handschriften, S. 313: under \ldblquote B.H. 13\rdblquote  he writes: \ldblquote {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930gi/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Sefer ha-Ge'ula}}\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (Buch der Erl\u246 \'f6sung), verfasst von {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[2].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 R. Abraham Abulafia}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , ein Kommentar zu den Geheimnissen von {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[1].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Maimonides'}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[1].6930gi/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 More Newuchim}}\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (B.H. 13), Abschrift durch R. Adonja ben Abba Calomiti 1329, Saloniki.\rdblquote  [+ FN]]
\par \pard\fi0\li0\qj\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 p. 311: \u8222 \'84In Leipzig sind zwei Handschriften des F\u252 \'fchrers der Unschl\u252 \'fcssigen vorhanden. [\u8230 \'85] die zweite (B.H. 13) wurde von R. Adonja ben Abba Calomiti 1329 in Saloniki angefertigt.\ldblquote }

