\uc1
\pard\li1080\fi-360\jclisttab\tx0\qj\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 {\listtext\pard\plain\f1\fs24\lang1033 \'96\tab}\ls1\ilvl1 {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f3\lang1037\fs24\chcbpat17 \u1505 \'f1\u1508 \'f4\u1512 \'f8 \u1499 \'eb\u1493 \'e5\u1493 \'e5\u1504 \'f0\u1493 \'e5\u1514 \'fa \u1492 \'e4\u1508 \'f4\u1497 \'e9\u1500 \'ec\u1493 \'e5\u1505 \'f1\u1493 \'e5\u1508 \'f4\u1497 \'e9\u1501 \'ed \u1500 \'ec\u1502 \'ee\u1506 \'f2\u1493 \'e5\u1500 \'ec\u1492 \'e4 \u1492 \'e4\u1497 \'e9\u1511 \'f7\u1512 \'f8 \u1492 \'e4\u1504 \'f0\u1499 \'eb\u1489 \'e1\u1491 \'e3 \u1488 \'e0\u1489 \'e1\u1493 \'e5 \u1495 \'e7\u1502 \'ee\u1488 \'e0\u1491 \'e3 \u1488 \'e0\u1500 \'ec\u1490 \'e2\u1494 \'e6\u1500 \'ec\u1497 \'e9}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (fol. 1v \endash  19v); \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 no marked beginning (title) and no marked ending (colophon etc.);\plain \f4\fs24  book about the opinions (\u8222 \'84de opinionibus\ldblquote ) of the philosophers by {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[0].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f4\fs24\chcbpat17 Ab\u363 u \u7716 ?\u257 amid al-Ghaz\u257 al\u299 i}}\plain \f4\fs24  (d. 1111), an almost literal translation of the Arabic original {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[1].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f4\fs24\chcbpat17 \u1605 ?\u1602 ?\u1575 ?\u1589 ?\u1583 ? \u1575 ?\u1604 ?\u1601 ?\u1604 ?\u1575 ?\u1587 ?\u1601 ?\u1577 ?}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (\u8222 \'84aims of the philosophers\ldblquote ); contains commentaries which are placed below every chapter; displayed is only the name of the commentator:
\plain\par \pard\fi0\li0\qj\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   \plain \f3\lang1037\fs24 \u1502 \'ee\u1513 \'f9\u1492 \'e4 \u1489 \'e1\u1503 \'ef \u1497 \'e9\u1492 \'e4\u1493 \'e5\u1513 \'f9\u1493 \'e5\u1506 \'f2\u1492 \'e4 \u1489 \'e1''\u1492 \'e4 \u1497 \'e9\u1513 \'f9\u1497 \'e9 \u1506 \'f2\u1502 \'ee''\u1492 \'e4\u1503 \'ef\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  ; other codices reveal that one is the translator and the other the author of the commentaries (\u8222 \'84Alii vero codices indicant, alium esse interpretem, alium commentariorum auctorem.\ldblquote ); codices from de Rossi name {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[1].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Jehuda ben Salomo Natan}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  as the translator (\u8222 \'84translatorem\ldblquote ) ofof the work from Arabic about whom nothing is know among the bibliographers, in case he is not accidentally the same as the translator (\u8222 \'84interpres\ldblquote )\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[2].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Ben Gudas Na}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ... [rest is missing]. The author of the commentary is {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[3].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Mose ben Josua}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , i. e. Moses Narbonis (1300-1362) alias Mose ben Josua ben Isai ben David, who gave the translated work of al-Gha\plain \f4\fs24 z\u257 al\u299 i a new preface and enriched it with descriptions/illustrations put underneath the text of the author. [\u8230 \'85comment on the error of Sabatai of ascribing the translation of the book to Moses Narbonis as well...]
\par \pard\fi0\li0\qj\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 State of preservation: mutilated in the end of the codex \u8594 ? thus it contains only the first part of the book (\u8222 \'84doctrina logica\ldblquote ) and a fragment of the second book (\u8222 \'84metaphysica\ldblquote )}

