\pard\li720\fi-360\jclisttab\tx0\qj\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 {\listtext\pard\plain\f1\fs24\lang1033 -\tab}\ls5\ilvl0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f3\fs24\chcbpat17 \u1497 ?\u1505 ?\u1493 ?\u1491 ? \u1502 ?\u1492 ?''\u1512 ?\u1512 ?\u1497 ? \u1502 ?\u1491 ?\u1493 ?\u1497 ?\u1488 ?\u1512 ?\u1503 ? \u1494 ?''\u1500 ?}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (fol. 99-171; digitized images: fol. 103r-175r), with many comments (\u8230 \'85); according to Delitzsch \ldblquote \plain \f3\fs24 \u1502 ?\u1492 ?''\u1512 ?\u1512 ?\u1497 ?\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \rdblquote  stands for Isaak Durensis (GND: {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[1].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Yits\u7717 ?a\u7731 ? ben Me\u702 ?ir, mi-Dura, 1033880833}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ;\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 active ca. 2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs16 nd\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  half of the 13\plain \f1\lang1033\fs16 th\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  century); \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 no obviously marked beginning;
\plain\par \pard\fi0\li720\qj\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8594 ? \plain \f3\fs24 \u1512 ?\u1489 ?\u1497 ? \u1497 ?\u1510 ?\u1495 ?\u1511 ? \u1489 ?\u1503 ? \u1512 ?\u1489 ?\u1497 ? \u1502 ?\u1488 ?\u1497 ?\u1512 ? \u1492 ?\u1500 ?\u1493 ?\u1497 ? \u1502 ?\u1491 ?\u1493 ?\u1512 ?\u1488 ?\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ; author of the halakhic work Sha\u703 ?arei Dura (\plain \f6\b\lang1037\fs24 \u1513 \'f9\u1506 \'f2\u1512 \'f8\u1497 \'e9 \u1491 \'e3\u1493 \'e5\u1512 \'f8\u1488 \'e0\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ); the present codex represents a compendium/excerpts of his work \plain \f3\fs24 \u1513 ?\u1506 ?\u1512 ?\u1497 ? \u1491 ?\u1493 ?\u1512 ?\u1488 ?\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  alias known as \u8222 \'84Fundamentum\ldblquote  (\plain \f3\fs24 \u1497 ?\u1505 ?\u1493 ?\u1491 ?\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) and \u8222 \'84Forbidden and Allowed\ldblquote  
\par \pard\fi0\li720\qj\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 (\plain \f3\fs24 \u1488 ?\u1497 ?\u1505 ?\u1493 ?\u1512 ? \u1493 ?\u1492 ?\u1497 ?\u1514 ?\u1512 ?\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) [v. i. David]; Sha\u703 ?arei Dura was printed several times, just like the ms. Cracov. 1534 (Catal. Oppenh., p. 47b). The fragment corresponds to the fifth book of the second part of Maimonides\rquote  \ldblquote Mishne\rdblquote  which treats the forbidden food, the laws of kosher butchering etc., too.}

