\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f3\fs24 1r-131v: \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 content:
\par \pard\li720\fi-360\jclisttab\tx0\qj\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 {\listtext\pard\plain\f5\fs24\lang1024 \u-4051 ?\tab}\ls3\ilvl0 kabbalistic work by an unknown author (according to Delitzsch it has to be distinguished from other works with similar titles) \endash  passages of the {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 \ldblquote Gale Razaja\rdblquote }}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  are cited and excerpted in another work (\ldblquote Gale Razaja is [\u8230 \'85] citatur et excerpitur in Jalquth Rubeni [\u8230 \'85]. Textum autem, quem Jalquth affert, ab hoc Ms. non differre affirmant {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[2].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Wagenseilius}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  [\u8230 \'85] et Goetzius [\u8230 \'85].\ldblquote )
\plain\par \pard\li1080\fi-360\jclisttab\tx0\qj\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 {\listtext\pard\plain\f5\fs24\lang1024 \u-4051 ?\tab}\ls3\ilvl1 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 about the author: the author is not mentioned in the book, but according to {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[1].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 \u8222 \'84Noblot Chokma\ldblquote }}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (\plain \f2\lang1037\fs24 \u1504 \'f0\u1493 \'e5\u1489 \'e1\u1500 \'ec\u1493 \'e5\u1514 \'fa \u1495 \'e7\u1499 \'eb\u1502 \'ee\u1492 \'e4\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) it is {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[0].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 R. Abraham ha-Levi}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , a disciple of {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[1].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Isaac Luria}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (\u8222 \'84Auctor libri Gale Razaja anonymus, qui [\u8230 \'85] est R. Abraham [\u8230 \'85] ha-Levi, discipulus Isaaci Luriae [\u8230 \'85].\rdblquote )}

