\par \pard\li720\fi-360\jclisttab\tx0\qj\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 {\listtext\pard\plain\f1\fs24\lang1033 -\tab}\ls2\ilvl0 {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Siddur}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  and a short {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[1].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Machzor}}
\plain\par {\listtext\pard\plain\f1\fs24\lang1033 -\tab}\ls2\ilvl0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 the spine (?) of the book (\ldblquote dorsum tegminis hujus codicis\rdblquote ) contains a little part of a commentary on Nehemia
\plain\par {\listtext\pard\plain\f1\fs24\lang1033 -\tab}\ls2\ilvl0 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 the Siddur starts (maybe) on fol. 129v \endash  cf. inscription on the upper margin \u8222 \'84\plain \f2\i\lang1037\fs24 \u1500 \'ec\u1513 \'f9\u1489 \'e1\u1514 \'fa \u1489 \'e1\u1512 \'f8\u1488 \'e0\u1513 \'f9\u1497 \'e9\u1514 \'fa\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 \ldblquote  (\u8222 \'84for the Shabbat of Bereshit\ldblquote ) - ?!}

