\pard\fi0\li720\qj\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f2\lang1033\fs24 history:
\par \pard\li720\fi-360\jclisttab\tx0\qj\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 {\listtext\pard\plain\f2\fs24\lang1033 -\tab}\ls2\ilvl0 scribe (of the first book): {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[0].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1037\fs24\chcbpat17 \u1506 \'f2\u1501 \'ed \u1492 \'e4\u1488 \'e0\u1512 \'f8\u1509 \'f5 \u1491 \'e3\u1488 \'e0\u1493 \'e5\u1512 \'f8\u1497 \'e9\u1514 \'fa\u1488 \'e0}}\plain \f2\lang1033\fs24  (\u8230 \'85de\rquote orayta), unexperienced and ignorant of the law; completion (of the first book): 16\plain \f2\lang1033\fs16 th\plain \f2\lang1033\fs24  c.
\plain\par {\listtext\pard\plain\f2\fs24\lang1033 -\tab}\ls2\ilvl0 \plain \f2\lang1033\fs24 scribe (of the second book): {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[1].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f3\fs24\chcbpat17 Josef ben Baruch Haas}}\plain \f2\lang1033\fs24  (v. colophon), born in Kol\u237 \'edn (Bohemia), in the area (\u8222 \'84pago\ldblquote ) of Schwarzenau (? \u8222 \'84Schwarzenaviae\ldblquote ) on the Danube, wrote it in 1537 for the use of {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[2].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f3\fs24\chcbpat17 Josef ha-Levi Zoref from Schwarzig}}\plain \f2\lang1033\fs24  (? \u8222 \'84Schwarzigiensis\ldblquote ); on the same page (the one with the colophon) there is a certificate of experience and industriousness for the butcher {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[3].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f3\fs24\chcbpat17 Salomon bar Levi}}\plain \f2\lang1033\fs24 , issued by {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[4].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f3\fs24\chcbpat17 Rabbi Salomon ben Isaac Einstedt }}\plain \f2\lang1033\fs24 from Fulda in 1555; ibidem a later possessor of this manuscript who also added a little picture on the front side of the first book (\plain \f1\lang1037\fs24 \u1502 \'ee\u1504 \'f0\u1492 \'e4\u1490 \'e2\u1497 \'e9\u1501 \'ed\plain \f2\lang1033\fs24 ) inscribed his name: {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[5].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f3\fs24\chcbpat17 Eliezer bar Josef ha-Levi ha-Zoref}}\plain \f2\lang1033\fs24  [possibly the son of the above mentioned Josef ha-Levi Zoref]}

