\uc1
\pard\fi0\li720\qj\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f3\lang1033\fs24 content:
\par \pard\li720\fi-360\jclisttab\tx0\qj\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 {\listtext\pard\plain\f3\fs24\lang1033 -\tab}\ls4\ilvl0 contains two books:
\plain\par \pard\li1440\fi-360\jclisttab\tx0\qj\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 {\listtext\pard\plain\f3\fs24\lang1033 1.\tab}\ls4\ilvl1 {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f2\lang1037\fs24\chcbpat17  \u1502 \'ee\u1504 \'f0\u1492 \'e4\u1490 \'e2\u1497 \'e9\u1501 \'ed}}\plain \f3\lang1033\fs24  (fol. 1r-53v), book about annual fixed ceremonies, religious customs (? \ldblquote religionibus\rdblquote ) and doctrines (? \ldblquote institutis\rdblquote ) which are supposed to be observed every year on single sacred days (\ldblquote holidays\rdblquote ?) when it is customary to go to the Synagogue; German rite (+ \ldblquote recenti\rdblquote ) which is not different from the one today [i. e. in the 19\plain \f3\lang1033\fs16 th\plain \f3\lang1033\fs24  c.]; start at new moon of Nissan and finishes with \ldblquote Parsot Sheqalim\rdblquote  and the new moon of Adar;  \u8230 \'85; \plain \f3\i\lang1033\fs24 fol. 1 is written on another paper; fol. 1r exhibits only the title of the work; fol. 1v is left blank; fol. 2 is written in another hand; fol. 53v does not show an obviously marked ending of the text}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg0\uc1\deff0\deflang0\deflangfe0{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset1 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset177 Times New Roman;}{\f2\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green255\blue255;\red0\green255\blue0;\red255\green0\blue255;\red255\green0\blue0;\red255\green255\blue0;\red255\green255\blue255;\red0\green0\blue128;\red0\green128\blue128;\red0\green128\blue0;\red128\green0\blue128;\red128\green0\blue0;\red128\green128\blue0;\red128\green128\blue128;\red192\green192\blue192;\red204\green238\blue221;}

\uc1
\pard\fi-360\li1440\qj\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1037\fs24 2. {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1037\fs24\chcbpat17 \u1513 \'f9\u1495 \'e7\u1497 \'e9\u1496 \'e8\u1493 \'e5\u1514 \'fa \u1493 \'e5\u1489 \'e1\u1491 \'e3\u1497 \'e9\u1511 \'f7\u1493 \'e5\u1514 \'fa}}\plain \f2\lang1033\fs24  (fol. 54r-61v), book on the animals which have to be butchered and examined according to the (Jewish) ritual; \plain \f2\i\lang1033\fs24 the title on fol. 54r was only later added with a pencil; fol. 53a (with the title written on the recto) is probably a later addition, too, since the paper is also much lighter}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg0\uc1\deff0\deflang0\deflangfe0{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset1 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset1 Times New Roman;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green255\blue255;\red0\green255\blue0;\red255\green0\blue255;\red255\green0\blue0;\red255\green255\blue0;\red255\green255\blue255;\red0\green0\blue128;\red0\green128\blue128;\red0\green128\blue0;\red128\green0\blue128;\red128\green0\blue0;\red128\green128\blue0;\red128\green128\blue128;\red192\green192\blue192;\red204\green238\blue221;}

