\pard\li1080\fi-360\jclisttab\tx0\qj\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 {\listtext\pard\plain\f5\fs24\lang1024 \u-4051 ?\tab}\ls3\ilvl1 {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930gi/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1037\fs24\chcbpat17 \u1488 \'e0\u1490 \'e2\u1512 \'f8\u1514 \'fa \u1500 \'ec\u1495 \'e7\u1499 \'eb\u1502 \'ee\u1497 \'e9 \u1502 \'ee\u1512 \'f8\u1513 \'f9''\u1497 \'e9\u1500 \'ec\u1497 \'e9\u1488 \'e0}}\plain \f2\lang1033\fs24  (fol. 19v \endash  23r, middle \u8594 ? in the manuscript the title \ldblquote \plain \f1\lang1037\fs24 \u1488 \'e0\u1497 \'e9\u1490 \'e2\u1512 \'f8\u1514 \'fa\plain \f2\lang1033\fs24 \rdblquote  is found on top of fol. 20r! \u8594 ? 20r-23r, middle), letter from {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[0].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f2\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Mose Maimonides}}\plain \f2\lang1033\fs24  to the people from Marseille (\u8222 \'84Massilienses\ldblquote ) [vgl. David] about astrology; but according to Delitzsch there is another title here which reads \u8222 \'84\plain \f1\lang1037\fs24 \u1492 \'e4\u1512 \'f8\u1491 \'e3\u1497 \'e9\u1501 \'ed \u1489 \'e1\u1502 \'ee\u1491 \'e3\u1497 \'e9\u1504 \'f0\u1514 \'fa \u1502 \'ee\u1504 \'f0\u1514 \'fa\u1508 \'f4''\u1513 \'f9\u1500 \'ec\u1497 \'e9\u1512 \'f8\plain \f2\lang1033\fs24 \ldblquote , thus it is a letter to the inhabitants of the city of Montpellier; added in the end is a story about \u8222 \'84Pseudomesia\ldblquote  [Pseudomessias?] who had been killed by the king of the Arabs;}

