\pard\fi0\li0\qj\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 history:
\par \pard\li720\fi-360\jclisttab\tx0\qj\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 {\listtext\pard\plain\f3\fs24\lang1024 \u-4051 ?\tab}\ls3\ilvl0 Delitzsch estimates that the codex is probably as old as the [Codex] \u8222 \'84Parisinus\ldblquote  which was finished in 1297; the age can be deduced from the secondary entries (tables attesting selling) inscribed in the end:
\plain\par \pard\li1080\fi-360\jclisttab\tx0\qj\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 {\listtext\pard\plain\f3\fs24\lang1024 \u-4051 ?\tab}\ls3\ilvl1 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 previous owners: \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24 1. {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[0].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Samuel ben Judah}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  sold this codex to \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24 2. {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[1].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Isaac ben Kalonymos}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  in the year 5070 i. e. 1310 in Bolsena (+\u8222 \'84Volsinii ad lacum Volsiniensem (Bolsena, lago di Bolsena); then \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24 3. {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[2].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 David ben Mose from Cracow}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  bought it in Venice; in the end of the commentary on the Minor Prophets there is a note that attests to the sale of the book together with three other books ({\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930gi/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 \u8222 \'84Machberet Menahem (ben Saruq)\ldblquote }}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[1].6930gi/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 \u8222 \'84Hasagot Dunas ben Librat\ldblquote }}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[2].6930gi/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 \u8222 \'84Sefer Nitzachon\ldblquote }}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (v. s.)) from \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24 4. {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[3].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Isaac ben Yequtiel}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  to \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24 5. {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[4].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Juda L\u246 \'f6b ben Mose Eleutheropolitanus}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  for four Polish gold pieces in 1592; \u8222 \'84a little later\ldblquote  (\u8222 \'84paullo post\ldblquote ) it came into the possession of \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24 6. {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[5].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Wagenseil}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  who mentions it in his book \u8222 \'84Tela ignea Satanae\ldblquote 
\plain\par \pard\li720\fi-360\jclisttab\tx0\qj\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 {\listtext\pard\plain\f3\fs24\lang1024 \u-4051 ?\tab}\ls3\ilvl0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 author: according to Bernardo de Rossi the author, {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[6].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Jesaia}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , lived in the end of the twelfth century, and bore the honorific titles \u8222 \'84ha-rishon\ldblquote  (\u8222 \'84\plain \f2\lang1037\fs24 \u1492 \'e4\u1512 \'f8\u1488 \'e0\u1513 \'f9\u1493 \'e5\u1503 \'ef\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \ldblquote ) and \u8222 \'84ha-ga'on\ldblquote  (\u8222 \'84\plain \f2\lang1037\fs24 \u1492 \'e4\u1490 \'e2\u1488 \'e0\u1493 \'e5\u1503 \'ef\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \ldblquote ), ancestor of the later Jesaia, Jesaia \u8222 \'84ha-acharon\ldblquote  (\u8222 \'84\plain \f2\lang1037\fs24 \u1492 \'e4\u1488 \'e0\u1495 \'e7\u1512 \'f8\u1493 \'e5\u1503 \'ef\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \ldblquote ); David Conforti ascribed the commentaries to Jesaia Tranensis (Isaia of Trani)
\plain\par {\listtext\pard\plain\f3\fs24\lang1024 \u-4051 ?\tab}\ls3\ilvl0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 probable copyist (\u8222 \'84\plain \f2\lang1037\fs24 \u1502 \'ee\u1506 \'f2\u1514 \'fa\u1497 \'e9\u1511 \'f7\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \ldblquote ) who also added comments to Isaia's notes: Zedekia
\plain\par \pard\fi-360\li720\qj\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\qj\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 AD, p. 309: \u8222 \'84Kommentar zu verschiedenen B\u252 \'fcchern der Bibel (Pentateuch, Propheten, Psalmen und Hiob): Der Kommentar wurde von einem gewissen R. Isaia verfasst, bei dem es sich um R. {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[6].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Isaia ben Mali von Trani}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  handeln k\u246 \'f6nnte, der im 12. und 13. Jahrhundert in Italien lebte. Die Abschrift k\u246 \'f6nnte im 13. Jahrhundert entstanden sein, ohne dass dies abschlie\u223 \'dfend gekl\u228 \'e4rt w\u228 \'e4re (B.H. 8. 41).\ldblquote }

