\pard\fi0\li720\qj\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 content:
\par \pard\li720\fi-360\jclisttab\tx0\qj\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 {\listtext\pard\plain\f1\fs24\lang1033 -\tab}\ls2\ilvl0 {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6922/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 commentaries on the Pentateuch}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  by Nachmanides (GND: {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[0].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Nachmanides, Moses; 118586157}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) who finished it in 1268;
\plain\par \pard\li1440\fi-360\jclisttab\tx0\qj\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 {\listtext\pard\plain\f1\fs24\lang1033 1.\tab}\ls2\ilvl1 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 the beginning until the Parasha Toledot is cut out (\ldblquote desecatum\rdblquote  [sic!] \u8594 ? \u8222 \'84desectum\ldblquote ?), thus the name of the author is not mentioned but can be concluded [by Delitzsch] from the works mentioned and the style of writing
\plain\par {\listtext\pard\plain\f1\fs24\lang1033 2.\tab}\ls2\ilvl1 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 it is an abbreviated version (\u8222 \'84compendiolum\ldblquote ) of Nachmanides' commentary on the Torah, that can be found in many manuscripts, even if they might not explicitly profess it. (\u8222 \'84Est igitur compendiolum vel anthologia ex auctoris \plain \f2\lang1037\fs24 \u1495 \'e7\u1497 \'e9\u1491 \'e3\u1493 \'e5\u1513 \'f9\u1497 \'e9\u1501 \'ed \u1489 \'e1\u1508 \'f4\u1497 \'e9\u1512 \'f8\u1493 \'e5\u1513 \'f9\u1497 \'e9 \u1492 \'e4\u1514 \'fa\u1493 \'e5\u1512 \'f8\u1492 \'e4\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  collecta, qualem multi codices, veluti [\u8230 \'85], cum diserte non profiteantur, exhibent.\ldblquote  \u8230 \'85)
\plain\par {\listtext\pard\plain\f1\fs24\lang1033 3.\tab}\ls2\ilvl1 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 it finishes without a colophon (\u8222 \'84clausula\ldblquote ), just with the word \u8222 \'84\plain \f2\lang1037\fs24 \u1495 \'e7\u1494 \'e6\u1511 \'f7\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \ldblquote 
\plain\par {\listtext\pard\plain\f1\fs24\lang1033 4.\tab}\ls2\ilvl1 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 there are glosses on the margin by an unknown author; on fol. 23r you find the inscription:}

